[FINDING B1] CI "Schema drift check" step FAILS on a clean tree.
  Command: diff <(tail -n +1 /tmp/schema.json) <(head -c -1 schema/agentteam.schema.json)
  Committed file ends with "}\n"; generated ends with "}\n" (identical).
  `head -c -1` strips the committed trailing newline, so diff reports a
  spurious trailing-newline difference => non-zero exit => CI step red even
  with zero drift. The one CI gate enforcing schema parity (python side) is broken.

[FINDING B2] `karo compile` crashes in default (yaml) mode.
  RepresenterError: ('cannot represent an object', <Backend.file: 'file'>)
  cli.py:121 calls yaml.safe_dump(doc, ...) on a doc containing pydantic enum
  objects. `karo compile --format json` works (uses kr.canonical_json). M0 command broken.

[FINDING B3] JSON Schema contains NO if/then cross-field rules (only pydantic
  anyOf for optionals). §4.3 conditional rules (lead-iff-pattern, pipeline.stages,
  prompt+autonomous, budget math, guard matcher) live ONLY in Python validate.py.
  The operator's CRD therefore does not enforce them => CLI-accepts/operator-accepts
  divergence; the "shared schema expresses if/then" claim (validate.py:5, §4.3) is unmet.

